<section class="st-hero"><svg class="st-hero-s" viewBox="0 0 1440 900" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M-40 120 C 300 40, 520 300, 720 260 S 1100 60, 1480 220"/><path d="M-40 760 C 280 840, 560 620, 760 700 S 1160 860, 1480 720" class="s2"/></svg><div class="st-w st-hero-g"><div class="st-hero-t"><p class="st-ey">The maison of straps</p><h1><span>Strap</span><span><i>py</i></span></h1><p class="st-hero-p">An independent guide to the strap: the quiet detail that decides how a bag is carried, how it hangs and how it feels at the end of the day.</p><a class="st-btn" href="#studio">Enter the strap studio</a></div><div class="st-oval"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1789110854914-000c8af68b3a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=900&q=75" alt="a person in a denim dress holding a yellow bag on a chain strap" width="700" height="900" fetchpriority="high"><span class="st-oval-r" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></section>

<section class="st-s st-in"><div class="st-w st-in-g"><p class="st-big rv">A bag is only as comfortable as its strap. Width, drop, material and hardware decide <em>everything</em> about how it wears.</p><div class="st-in-n stg"><div class="rv"><b data-count="5">5</b><span>strap styles every wardrobe uses</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="4">4</b><small>cm</small><span>a wide strap spreads the weight</span></div><div class="rv"><b data-count="120">120</b><small>cm</small><span>a typical crossbody strap</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="st-s st-sty" id="styles"><div class="st-w st-sty-g"><div><p class="st-ey">The strap index</p><h2 class="rv">Five ways to carry</h2><p class="st-p">Hover a name to see the strap. On a phone, tap it.</p></div><ul class="st-list" id="st-list"><li class="st-li" data-i="0"><span>01</span><b>The chain</b><em>Metal links, often threaded with leather. Evening-ready and surprisingly strong.</em></li><li class="st-li" data-i="1"><span>02</span><b>The top handle</b><em>Short and structured, carried in the hand or the crook of the arm.</em></li><li class="st-li" data-i="2"><span>03</span><b>The crossbody</b><em>Long and adjustable, worn across the body for hands-free days.</em></li><li class="st-li" data-i="3"><span>04</span><b>The shoulder strap</b><em>A medium drop that tucks the bag neatly under the arm.</em></li><li class="st-li" data-i="4"><span>05</span><b>The convertible</b><em>Detachable hooks let one bag change its strap with your plans.</em></li></ul></div><div class="st-fl" id="st-fl" aria-hidden="true"><div class="st-fl-i" data-i="0"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1781751594989-ac3ad190db3c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a black quilted bag with a chain strap" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="st-fl-i" data-i="1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1663705828016-4a45995ad32a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a person holding a black bag by its strap" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="st-fl-i" data-i="2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1761275398406-fe000b95621e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a black leather crossbody bag on a table" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="st-fl-i" data-i="3"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1765114470103-b68286cf9c6d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a woman in a white cardigan holding a shoulder bag" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></div><div class="st-fl-i" data-i="4"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1654707633360-1e2bbf09a406?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=520&q=75" alt="a green bag with its strap hanging from a chair" width="420" height="520" loading="lazy"></div></div><div class="st-w st-sty-m" id="st-m" aria-live="polite"></div></section>

<section class="st-s st-std" id="studio"><div class="st-w st-std-g"><div class="st-std-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 360 380" id="sd-svg" aria-hidden="true"></svg></div><div><p class="st-ey">Interactive</p><h2 class="rv">The strap studio</h2><p class="st-p">Choose a bag, a strap and a colour. See how the strap changes the whole character of the bag.</p><fieldset class="st-fs"><legend>Bag</legend><div class="st-chips"><label><input type="radio" name="sb" value="0" checked><span>Saddle</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sb" value="1"><span>Box</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sb" value="2"><span>Pouch</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="st-fs"><legend>Strap</legend><div class="st-chips"><label><input type="radio" name="ss" value="0" checked><span>Fine leather</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ss" value="1"><span>Chain</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ss" value="2"><span>Wide woven</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ss" value="3"><span>Top handle</span></label></div></fieldset><fieldset class="st-fs"><legend>Colour</legend><div class="st-sw"><label><input type="radio" name="sc" value="#4E1820" checked><span style="background:#4E1820" title="Oxblood"></span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sc" value="#1E1C1B"><span style="background:#1E1C1B" title="Black"></span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sc" value="#B88A5E"><span style="background:#B88A5E" title="Tan"></span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sc" value="#D9B9AE"><span style="background:#D9B9AE" title="Blush"></span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sc" value="#3F5A4A"><span style="background:#3F5A4A" title="Forest"></span></label></div></fieldset><p class="st-std-o" id="sd-o" aria-live="polite"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="st-col"><div class="st-col-c st-col-a" id="col-a"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1709899373206-26c623817a49?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a person carrying a black bag on a long strap" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1597633244018-0201d0158aab?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a brown leather sling bag hanging outdoors" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="st-col-m"><p class="st-ey">On the move</p><h2 class="rv">Worn, not just owned</h2><p class="st-p">The best straps disappear into the day: the right length, the right weight, never in the way.</p></div><div class="st-col-c st-col-b" id="col-b"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1780355772244-4eedc2e3cd41?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a woman crouching on asphalt with a bag" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617636521236-db69104aa220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a patchwork denim tote bag with a strap" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="st-s st-care"><div class="st-w st-care-g"><div><p class="st-ey">Strap care</p><h2 class="rv">Small habits, longer life</h2></div><div class="st-acc"><details open><summary>Leather straps</summary><p>Wipe with a soft, dry cloth after wear. Condition two or three times a year, testing on the underside first, and let the strap rest flat if it starts to twist.</p></details><details><summary>Chain straps</summary><p>Wipe with a dry cloth to remove skin oils, store the chain inside the bag to stop it scratching the leather, and keep away from perfume.</p></details><details><summary>Fabric and woven straps</summary><p>Brush off dust, spot clean with a damp cloth and mild soap, and dry flat away from heat so the weave keeps its shape.</p></details><details><summary>Hooks and hardware</summary><p>Check that clips close firmly and that rings have not opened. A loose swivel hook is a small repair; a lost bag is not.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="st-gl"><div class="st-w st-gl-g"><a class="st-gl-a rv" href="bag-strap-styles-guide.html"><div class="st-gl-i st-gl-n" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 200"><path d="M90 110C90 30 210 30 210 110" fill="none" stroke="#4E1820" stroke-width="5"/><rect x="60" y="105" width="180" height="80" rx="14" fill="#4E1820"/><circle cx="150" cy="140" r="8" fill="#B8934A"/></svg></div><span>Guide I</span><b>Bag Strap Styles</b><em>Chain, top handle, crossbody, shoulder and convertible.</em></a><a class="st-gl-a rv" href="strap-care-guide.html"><div class="st-gl-i st-gl-n" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 200"><path d="M40 60 C 120 0, 180 160, 260 80" fill="none" stroke="#B8934A" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="40" cy="60" r="12" fill="none" stroke="#4E1820" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="260" cy="80" r="12" fill="none" stroke="#4E1820" stroke-width="4"/></svg></div><span>Guide II</span><b>Strap Care &amp; Fit</b><em>Width, drop and how to keep every strap at its best.</em></a></div></section>

